-- Restamp the two derivation_sha values that no longer verify (K01).
--
-- WHY THESE ARE WRONG
-- assess_cell.sha() hashes item_code|population_code|sorted(governing_refs)
-- ::rule_version. It is a FINGERPRINT OF THE DETERMINATION'S INPUTS, not a
-- record that an engine process ran -- its own docstring says the point is that
-- "staleness stays checkable". So when a row's inputs change legitimately, the
-- fingerprint must follow, or the check it exists to serve reports nothing.
--
-- Both rows changed for ordinary, correct reasons and neither change restamped:
--
--   9007  B-10 x BRAIN.  Recorded sha b1a9c222... recomputes exactly as
--         sha("B-10","NEU",["REF-00537"]). The population code was renamed
--         NEU -> BRAIN and the hash kept attesting the old identity. The
--         rendered document carried the same fossil until 2026-08-04.
--
--   9003  G-03 x MOB.  Recorded sha ca3b869f... recomputes exactly as the hash
--         of the SIX-ref governing set ['REF-00053','REF-00054','REF-00055',
--         'REF-00056','REF-00057','REF-00058']. The evidence-auditor sweep in
--         data_20260804001923 removed REF-00055 and REF-00058 from this cell
--         under DR-2026-07-20 -- correctly -- without restamping. The set is
--         now four.
--
-- WHAT RESTAMPING DOES AND DOES NOT ASSERT
-- I argued in the K01 commit that restamping "asserts an engine derivation that
-- did not happen". That overstated it, and the owner ruling is right: the sha
-- is a function of the row, so recomputing it asserts only what the row now
-- says. What an engine did is recorded by rule_version, which is untouched
-- here -- both rows keep 'pilot-2', the version under which they were
-- determined. Restamping realigns the fingerprint with the inputs; it does not
-- claim the determination was re-derived.
--
-- WHAT THIS DOES NOT TOUCH
-- The 8 determinations carrying no sha at all (9008-9015) are left alone. They
-- were never stamped, and 9014/9015 have no rule_version to hash, so there is
-- nothing to realign -- that is a different question from a fingerprint that
-- drifted, and it is queued rather than answered here.
--
-- After this, K01 passes on 7 of 7 non-NULL shas and continues to report the 8
-- unattested rows without failing them.

